WEBVTT

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:07.490
&GT;&GT; GREAT.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:09.890
LET ME FIRST SAY GOOD MORNING
AND WELCOME.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:12.590
TODAY'S OVERSIGHT HEARING IS
INTENDED TO PROVIDE

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:15.740
MEMBERS OF THE COMMITTEE, AS
WELL AS THE PUBLIC,

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:19.370
WITH AN UPDATE FROM THE STATE'S
ENERGY AGENCIES

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:22.700
AND THE STATE'S PRINCIPAL
ELECTRICAL GRID OPERATOR,

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.910
ON THE EFFORTS TO ADDRESS
ELECTRICITY RELIABILITY

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:29.240
ASSOCIATED WITH MANAGING SUPPLY
AND DEMAND,

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.650
PARTICULARLY GIVEN EXTREME
WEATHER EVENTS AND AS

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.950
THE STATE TRANSITIONS TO ZERO
CARBON ENERGY.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:37.729
FUTURE.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.670
THIS IS A FOLLOW UP TO LAST
YEAR'S, UH,

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:42.740
SIMILARLY FOCUSED OVERSIGHT
HEARING,

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:45.080
AS WELL AS OVERSIGHT HEARING
PREVIOUSLY

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:46.820
HELD IN RECENT YEARS,

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:50.210
INCLUDING IN 2021, IN RESPONSE
TO

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:53.270
THE AUGUST 2020 UNEXPECTED
ELECTRICITY

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:56.000
ROTATING OUTAGES ORDERED BY THE
STATE'S

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.820
MAIN ELECTRICAL GRID OPERATOR,

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.350
THE CALIFORNIA INDEPENDENT
SYSTEMS

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.150
OPERATOR, OR CAL, ISO,

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:04.880
AND A HEARING IN 2022 REGARDING

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:06.890
THE PROPOSED EXTENSION OF

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:10.819
THE OPERATIONS OF DIABLO CANYON
NUCLEAR POWER PLANT,

00:01:10.819 --> 00:01:13.670
IN LARGE PART TO SUPPORT OUR
ELECTRICITY

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:15.440
SUPPLY RELIABILITY,

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:18.200
WHICH WE'VE PROVEN TO BE VERY
CRITICAL

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.640
AND NEEDED AT THIS TIME.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:21.920
SINCE 2020, WE HAVE EXPERIENCED

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.540
CHALLENGES TO ENSURING

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:26.990
RELIABILITY DURING SOME EXTREME
HEAT EVENTS,

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:29.690
PARTICULARLY IN THE EVENING
HOURS

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:31.400
IN THE LATE SUMMER MONTHS

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.350
WHEN RESIDENTS RELY ON AIR

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:35.090
CONDITIONING TO KEEP COOL.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:38.870
LAST YEAR, THE ISO ISSUED
EMERGENCY ALERTS

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:42.220
EARLIER IN THE SUMMER SO FAR
THIS SUMMER,

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:44.890
THERE HAVE NOT BEEN ANY
EMERGENCY

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:47.860
ALERTS ISSUED BY THE CAL ISO.

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:50.500
HOWEVER, LAST MONTH, THE ISO
ISSUED

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.750
SEVERAL DAYS OF NOTICES FOR

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:55.570
TRANSMISSION EMERGENCIES AND
RESTRICTED

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:57.460
MAINTENANCE OPERATIONS.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:01.090
THOSE SEEMINGLY MANAGED THESE
NOTICES

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:04.510
SERVE AS A REMINDER OF THE
IMPORTANCE

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:07.630
OF THE NEED TO REMAIN VIGILANT
AND ON

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:10.630
RELIABILITY OF THE ELECTRIC
GRID.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.820
WE KNOW THAT ELECTRICITY
OUTAGES,

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:14.590
DEPENDING ON THEIR SCALE,

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:17.860
DURATION AND FREQUENCY, CAN BE
LIFE THREATENING.

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:21.370
ELECTRICITY OUTAGES CAN BE
CAUSED BY

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:24.370
MANY ISSUES INCLUDED
DISTRIBUTION,

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.830
EQUIPMENT FAILURE, OR AS A
SAFETY

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:28.690
MEASURE SUCH AS PUBLIC SAFETY.

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:32.410
POWER SHUT OFFS WHEN WILDFIRE
RISKS ARE HIGH.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:36.040
TODAY'S HEARING IS FOCUSED ON
THE SUPPLY AND DEMAND

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.889
CHALLENGES OF BALANCING THE
ELECTRIC GRID.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:42.639
THE CHALLENGES TO ENSURING
RELIABILITY ARE SEVERAL

00:02:42.639 --> 00:02:45.700
AS TRANSITION TO ZERO CARBON
FUTURE,

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:50.080
INCLUDING A NEW MIX OF
GENERATION RESOURCES

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.690
SUPPLYING ELECTRICITY TO THE
ELECTRIC GRID,

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:57.610
INCLUDING A SIGNIFICANT PORTION
THAT ARE VARIABLE,

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.530
SUCH AS WIND AND SOLAR,

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:01.780
WHICH ARE NOT AVAILABLE AT ALL
TIMES,

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.000
INCLUDING DURING PEAK HOURS.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:07.000
THE DEPLOYMENT OF DISTRIBUTED
ENERGY RESOURCES

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.850
CAN HELP REDUCE THE DEMANDS ON
ELECTRIC GRID,

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:11.620
BUT CAN ALSO CONTRIBUTE TO

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:14.320
THE PEAK DEMAND AS THE ENERGY
FROM

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.900
DISTRIBUTED ENERGY RESOURCES

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.490
MAY NO LONGER BE GENERATING,

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:22.060
AND THESE CUSTOMERS MUST RELY ON
THE ELECTRIC GRID,

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:24.700
FOR EXAMPLE, ROOFTOP SOLAR
WITHOUT BATTERY BACKUP.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:28.030
LOCAL AND STATE POLICIES TO
MITIGATE

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:29.260
CLIMATE EMISSIONS ARE

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:31.330
DRIVING INCREASING ELECTRICITY

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:33.100
DEMAND, QUITE LITERALLY,

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:36.460
AS THE TRANSPORTATION AND
BUILDING SECTORS

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:38.140
ARE INCREASINGLY REQUIRED TO
SHIFT

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:41.560
AWAY FROM FOSSIL FUELS TO
CLEANER CARBON SOURCES,

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:43.420
ESPECIALLY ELECTRICITY.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:46.000
THE GROWING DEVELOPMENT OF
ARTIFICIAL

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.130
INTELLIGENCE IS FURTHER
INCREASING

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:49.810
ELECTRICITY DEMANDS NEEDED TO

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:52.120
OPERATE COMPUTING SYSTEMS.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.240
STATE POLICIES THAT AUTHORIZE
LOCAL

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:57.490
GOVERNMENTS WHO ELECT AND,

00:03:57.490 --> 00:04:00.400
IN MORE LIMITED CASES, PRIVATE
COMPANIES.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:04.090
THE ABILITY TO PROCURE
ELECTRICITY RESOURCES

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.700
KNOWN AS A COMMUNITY CHOICE

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:10.030
AGGREGATORS OR CCAS AND ELECTRIC

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:12.610
SERVICE PROVIDERS RESPECTIVELY,

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:15.550
RESULTING IN A FRAGMENTED
PROCUREMENT

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:16.990
LANDSCAPE THAT ADDS

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:19.270
COMPLICATIONS TOWARDS A SEAMLESS

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:20.470
TRANSITION TO MEETING

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:23.080
THE STATE'S RENEWABLE ENERGY
AND ZERO

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:25.330
CARBON ENERGY RESOURCES GOAL,

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:28.750
WHILE ENSURING ELECTRICITY
RELIABILITY.

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:31.390
ADDITIONALLY, THE CURRENT
TIGHTENING

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:33.550
OF RESOURCES ADEQUACY OR
RESOURCE

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:36.520
ADEQUACY MARKET WOULD
REQUIREMENTS

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:38.440
FOR PLANNING RESERVE MARGINS,

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:40.720
INCREASING THE STATE PROCUREMENT

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:43.120
RESOURCES TO SERVE AS INSURANCE,

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:45.880
AND LIMITED IMPORTS,
PARTICULARLY

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:48.580
THE LIMITED OUT OF STATE
HYDROPOWER

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:50.320
RESOURCES DUE TO DROUGHT
CONDITIONS

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:51.970
IN THE NORTH WEST AND CANADA,

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:53.350
SEEM TO BE FURTHER INCREASING

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:55.650
PRICES FOR ALL CUSTOMERS.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.870
AS I'VE SAID BEFORE,

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:01.290
WE'RE FLYING AN AIRPLANE WHILE
REDESIGNING IT,

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:03.120
ADDING PASSENGERS AND CHANGING

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.650
THE FUEL MIX MID-AIR

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.350
AS WEATHER FORECASTS CONSTANTLY
SHIFT,

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:10.230
REQUIRING ADJUSTMENTS TO THE
FLIGHT PATHS.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:12.450
IN RECENT YEARS, WE HAVE
APPROPRIATED

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.550
BILLIONS OF DOLLARS

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:18.060
OF STATE BUDGET TOWARD
ELECTRICITY RELIABILITY,

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.920
AUTHORIZED EXTENSION OF DIABLO

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.540
CANYON NUCLEAR POWER PLANT,

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:23.070
AND JUST LAST YEAR AUTHORIZED

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:23.940
THE DEPARTMENT OF WATER

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:26.490
RESOURCES TO SERVE AS A CENTRAL
PROCUREMENT

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:29.550
ENTITY SHOULD THE PUC IDENTIFY
A NEED

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:33.839
FOR A SPECIFIED LONG TIME
RESOURCES.

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:38.970
WHEN WE ARE IN OUR EFFORTS TO
ENSURE, I MEAN,

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:41.610
WHERE ARE WE IN OUR EFFORTS TO
ENSURE RELIABILITY?

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:45.180
WHAT'S OUR GAME PLAN TO ENSURE
THAT RELIABILITY

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:47.339
REMAINS AT THE FOREFRONT OF OUR
EFFORTS?

00:05:47.339 --> 00:05:50.310
AND EVEN AS WE TRANSITION TO
ZERO ENERGY

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:53.640
AND WORK TOWARD ENSURING
AFFORDABILITY?

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:55.770
ADDITIONALLY, I'VE ASKED THE
ADMINISTRATION

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:56.820
TO PROVIDE A BRIEF

00:05:56.820 --> 00:06:00.750
SUMMARY UPDATE OF THE WEST WIDE
PATHWAYS INITIATIVE,

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:03.930
AN EFFORT TO EXPAND ENERGY
MARKETS ACROSS THE WEST

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.960
CURRENTLY WITHIN THE LIMITS OF
EXISTING LAW.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:10.140
THE INTENT IS TO PROVIDE MEMBERS
WITH AN AWARENESS

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:11.970
AND UNDERSTANDING OF THE EFFORT,

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:13.950
THOUGH ADDITIONAL DISCUSSIONS

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:15.660
AND BRIEFINGS MAY BE NEEDED.

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:17.220
WITH ALL THAT BEING SAID,

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:19.860
NOW LET'S HEAR FROM OUR ENERGY
AGENCIES,

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:21.779
THE CALIFORNIA ENERGY
COMMISSION,

00:06:21.779 --> 00:06:24.000
THE CALIFORNIA PUBLIC UTILITIES
COMMISSION,

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.040
AS WELL AS THE DEPARTMENT OF
WATER RESOURCES

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:28.440
AND THE CALIFORNIA INDEPENDENT
SYSTEM OPERATOR.

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:31.080
I WANT TO SAY WELCOME, AND WE
WILL BEGIN WITH

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:35.040
OUR CALIFORNIA ENERGY VICE
