00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:34.560
RELIABILITY WITH MY COLLEAGUES

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:36.150
FROM THE ENERGY COMMISSION,

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:38.070
THE CALIFORNIA INDEPENDENT
SYSTEM OPERATOR

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:39.930
IN THE DEPARTMENT OF WATER
RESOURCES.

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:41.280
I'M GOING TO START US OFF,

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:44.600
AND THEN WE WILL ALL BE SHARING
THE EXPLANATION

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:45.890
OF A POWERPOINT PRESENTATION

00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:47.330
THAT WE HAVE FOR YOU TODAY.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.610
UM, WE'RE HERE TO TALK ABOUT
SUMMER

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:51.140
RELIABILITY READINESS,

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:53.360
BUT I WANT TO START WITH THE
BIG PICTURE,

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:56.000
TO PROVIDE SOME BACKGROUND TO
DESCRIBE

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:58.100
THE BACKGROUND IN WHICH WE'RE
WORKING.

00:07:58.280 --> 00:08:01.580
THE ELECTRIC SECTOR PLAYS A
CRITICAL ROLE

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:03.890
IN CALIFORNIA'S CLIMATE CHANGE
STRATEGY.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.230
WE'RE BOTH ELECTRIFYING THE
ECONOMY

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:09.500
AND DECARBONIZING THE SOURCES
OF GENERATION

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.110
TO SUPPLY ELECTRICITY FOR THE

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:15.560
THE NEW TYPES OF FUEL SWITCHING.

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:18.620
AND WE'RE THAT WE'RE DOING
THROUGHOUT OUR ECONOMY,

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:19.850
INCLUDING TRANSPORTATION,

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:22.550
ELECTRIFICATION AND BUILDING
ELECTRIFICATION.

00:08:22.670 --> 00:08:26.870
MUCH PROGRESS HAS BEEN MADE IN
THE ELECTRIC SECTOR,

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:28.610
AND IN 2022,

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:31.790
61% OF THE STATE'S ELECTRICITY
WAS GENERATED

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:34.490
BY RENEWABLE AND ZERO EMISSION
RESOURCES.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:36.380
WE ALSO ACHIEVED NEW RECORDS.

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:40.460
JUST THIS YEAR, WE HAD 146 DAYS
WHERE CLEAN

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:44.059
ENERGY EXCEEDED KAIZO CONSUMER
DEMAND.

00:08:44.059 --> 00:08:47.330
AT SOME POINT IN THE DAY, WE HAD
AN ALL TIME RECORD

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:52.130
IN SOLAR PRODUCTION PEAK WITH
19,368MW

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:56.840
ON JUNE 20TH AND THE KYSOW
FOOTPRINT IS APPROACHING

00:08:56.870 --> 00:09:00.559
TEN GIGAWATTS OF GRID SCALE
BATTERY CAPACITY.

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:03.679
SO WITH THIS MOMENTUM, WE'RE
WORKING TOWARDS

00:09:03.679 --> 00:09:05.780
THE GOALS SET BY THE LEGISLATURE

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:09.260
90% CLEAN ELECTRICITY SALES
BY 2035,

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:14.360
95% BY 2040, AND 100% BY 2045.

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:16.640
AT THE SAME TIME, WE'RE, OF
COURSE,

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:19.460
FIGHTING AGAINST THE IMPACTS OF
CLIMATE CHANGE.

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:21.770
CLIMATE CHANGE IS CAUSING
UNPRECEDENTED

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:23.090
STRESS ON OUR GRID.

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:24.950
EXTREME HEAT, DROUGHT,

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:27.440
FLOOD AND WILDFIRES ARE
INCREASING

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:30.620
IN FREQUENCY AND INTENSITY AND
THREATEN RELIABILITY.

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:33.590
THE FUTURE WHAT WE'RE ALL
WORKING TOWARDS

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:35.929
IS ONE THAT THAT IS CLEAN,

00:09:35.929 --> 00:09:38.179
SAFE, AFFORDABLE AND RELIABLE,

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:42.020
AND WITH CLEAR STATUTORY
DIRECTIVES AND RELATIVELY

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:44.480
LOW COST OPTIONS FOR CLEAN
ENERGY SUPPLY.

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:47.210
IT'S NOT A QUESTION OF IF, BUT
WHEN,

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:50.840
BUT HOW WE TRANSITION TO OUR
CLEAN ENERGY FUTURE.

00:09:50.870 --> 00:09:52.910
I'LL NOW TURN TO VICE CHAIR
GUNDA.

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:56.750
&GT;&GT; THANK YOU, PRESIDENT
REYNOLDS,

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:58.160
AND GOOD MORNING, CHAIR,

